Licences of the code a seams-core build compiles from chemfiles

seams-core itself is under the MIT licence; see LICENSE.

With chemfiles on (-Dwith_chemfiles=auto, the default, or enabled) and no
installed chemfiles that passes cmake/chemfiles_mmcif_probe.cpp, Meson and
CMake fetch chemfiles 0.10.4, apply cmake/patches/, and build
libseams-chemfiles. Meson installs it as libseams-chemfiles.so.0.10 beside
libyodaLib. That library holds compiled code from chemfiles and from the
libraries chemfiles bundles, each under its own licence, listed below. The
paths are inside the fetched chemfiles source; each archive in its
external/ directory unpacks to a directory of the same name. Only the
files the build compiles or includes are listed; the other files of those
archives stay in the build tree and are not distributed. AUTHORS names the
authors of each part.

The conditions on redistribution:

- All parts: keep the copyright notices and licence texts. A binary
  distribution reproduces them in its documentation. The BSD, NCSA and
  similar licences also forbid using a holder's name to endorse a derived
  product.
- gemmi (MPL-2.0): its files stay under MPL-2.0, and whoever ships them,
  also inside a binary, makes their source available under MPL-2.0.
- molfiles/src/abinitplugin.c: its author allows the code "for as long as
  it is part of an open source project" and does "not allow" it "to be
  part of any closed source project". The build compiles it.
- molfiles/src/ReadPARM.h and molfiles/src/ReadPARM7.h: their notice is
  kept unmodified and any change to the rest of the file is noted in
  comments. The build compiles them (parm and parm7 plugins).

seams-core is open source (MIT) and is not sold, which meets the ABINIT
condition. It binds anyone who redistributes a build that contains
libseams-chemfiles too: that build may not become part of closed-source
software.


chemfiles 0.10.4, with cmake/patches/chemfiles-0.10.4-*.patch
  License: BSD-3-Clause
  Text: LICENSE
  include/chemfiles/external/optional.hpp: BSL-1.0, text at the end of
    this file
  include/chemfiles/external/span.hpp: MIT, text in the file header
  include/chemfiles/external/string_view.hpp: BSL-1.0, text at the end
    of this file
  The patches in cmake/patches are by the d-SEAMS developers, under
  seams-core's MIT licence.

Libraries in external/ that the build compiles:

bzip2
  License: bzip2-1.0.6 (BSD-style)
  Text: bzip2/LICENSE
fmt
  License: MIT
  Text: fmt/LICENSE.rst
gemmi (headers; chemfiles' CIF and mmCIF readers include them)
  License: MPL-2.0, https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/
  gemmi/include/gemmi/third_party/tao (PEGTL): MIT, text in
    gemmi/include/gemmi/third_party/tao/LICENSE
lzma (liblzma)
  License: public domain
  Text: lzma/COPYING
mmtf-cpp (headers)
  License: MIT
  Text: mmtf-cpp/LICENSE
  cmake/patches/chemfiles-0.10.4-mmtf-sources.patch checks the binary
    decoder's lengths and integer arithmetic, and the length of a
    transform matrix.
  mmtf-cpp/msgpack-c: BSL-1.0, with its copies of Boost.Preprocessor and
    Boost.Predef, also BSL-1.0 (text at the end of this file). The same
    patch changes msgpack/v1/adaptor/carray.hpp, which converted an empty
    array through a null pointer; the file keeps its BSL-1.0 notice.
molfiles (VMD molfile plugins)
  License: University of Illinois Open Source License (NCSA), for every
    compiled file not listed below
  Text: molfiles/LICENSE
  Most files carry "(C) Copyright ... The Board of Trustees of the
  University of Illinois". Compiled files with no notice of their own
  (periodic_table.h, unit_conversion.h, vaspplugin.h, the five VASP
  plugins, vtfplugin.c, xsfplugin.cxx) are covered by molfiles/LICENSE
  as part of the plugin distribution.
  Compiled files under other terms, each with its text in its own header:
    molfiles/src/abinitplugin.c: Rob Lahaye's terms. The code may be
      included only while it is part of an open-source project, never in
      a closed-source one. There is no other licence text.
    molfiles/src/dmsplugin.cxx, molfiles/src/dtrplugin.cxx,
    molfiles/src/dtrplugin.hxx, molfiles/src/maeffplugin.cxx:
    BSD-3-Clause, Copyright 2009 D. E. Shaw Research, LLC. dmsplugin
    links the system SQLite3. SQLite is not compiled from this tree
    and its sources are not part of the vendored chemfiles.
    molfiles/src/ReadPARM.h, molfiles/src/ReadPARM7.h: Copyright 1992
      Regents of the University of California (Bill Ross, UCSF). They may
      be distributed if the notice is kept unmodified and changes to the
      rest of the file are noted in comments.
      cmake/patches/chemfiles-0.10.4-molfile-sources.patch bounds the
      %s scans in ReadPARM7.h, checks the reads, counts and indices of
      both readers, and notes those changes in each file.
  Compiled plugins (external/CMakeLists.txt after
  cmake/patches/chemfiles-0.10.4-molfiles.patch): abinitplugin,
  bgfplugin, binposplugin, carplugin, corplugin, cpmdlogplugin,
  cpmdplugin, cubeplugin, dlpolyplugin, dmsplugin, dtrplugin,
  gamessplugin, gaussianplugin, gromacsplugin, jsplugin, maeffplugin,
  mdfplugin, moldenplugin, namdbinplugin, parm7plugin, parmplugin,
  pqrplugin, psfplugin, rst7plugin, tinkerplugin, vasp5xdatcarplugin,
  vaspoutcarplugin, vaspposcarplugin, vaspxdatcarplugin, vaspxmlplugin,
  vtfplugin, xbgfplugin and xsfplugin, with hash.c and the headers they
  include. cpmdlogplugin and gaussianplugin are the CPMD and Gaussian
  log readers. Their sources were wrapped in `#if false` until
  molfile_plugin.h grew the three QM fields they write.
